#
# Backs up EVERY class of pLibRef into its per-library vault, and creates
# the folder structure alongside. Returns one protocol line; the per-class
# detail lands in the backup list with bytes and ticks.
#
# Folders do NOT go through $backupClass: that would find the folder in the
# vault, remove it and add it again, orphaning the classes inside. They go
# through $ensureFolder, which creates what is missing and touches nothing
# else. Folders carry 0 bytes anyway.
#
# ORDER IN THE LOOP MATTERS: elapsed is computed FIRST, then the cancel
# test, then the work. Computing it at the end left the test running
# against the previous round - and against an empty value in round 1.
#
# Cancel is tested BETWEEN classes only: Disable cancel test at loops inside
# a reversible block, so no class is ever left half written. Cancelling
# aborts the whole run - a skipped backup must not leave the script running
# unprotected. abs() because #CT wraps after about 414 days of uptime.
If isclear(pLibRef)
	Quit method 'backupLibrary: no library reference - nothing backed up. '
End If
Begin reversible block
	Disable cancel test at loops
End reversible block
Calculate startTicks as #CT
Calculate shown as kFalse
Calculate done as 0
Calculate skipped as 0
Calculate bytes as 0
Calculate elapsed as 0
Do pLibRef.$classes.$makelist($ref.$name,$ref.$classtype*1) Returns clist
Calculate total as clist.$linecount
For clist.$line from 1 to clist.$linecount step 1
	Calculate elapsed as abs(#CT-startTicks)
	If shown
		Redraw working message
		If canceled (No refresh)
			Close working message
			Calculate text as con('backupLibrary: CANCELLED after ',done,' of ',total,' - run NOT started. ')
			Do cBackups.$add(text,pLibRef.$name,pLibRef.$name,'',bytes,elapsed,'library')
			Quit method text
		End If
	Else
		If elapsed>120
			Working message Backup (Cancel button) {[pLibRef.$name]: [done] / [total]}
			Calculate shown as kTrue
		End If
	End If
	Calculate cName as clist.C1
	Set reference itemRef to pLibRef.$classes.$findname(cName)
	If itemRef
		If clist.C2=kFolder
			Do $cinst.$ensureFolder(itemRef.$ref)
			Calculate skipped as skipped+1
		Else
			Calculate bytes as bytes+itemRef.$disksize
			Calculate text as $cinst.$backupClass(itemRef.$ref)
			Calculate done as done+1
		End If
	End If
End For
If shown
	Close working message
End If
Calculate elapsed as abs(#CT-startTicks)
Calculate text as con('backupLibrary: ',pLibRef.$name,' - ',done,' classes, ',skipped,' folders, ',bytes,' bytes, ',elapsed,' ticks. ')
Do cBackups.$add(text,pLibRef.$name,pLibRef.$name,'',bytes,elapsed,'library')
Quit method text